@info
{
    name: "Time Crystal Neural Network in PLingua"
    version: "1.0.0"
    description: "P-Systems implementation of feedforward networks of time crystal neurons"
    author: "nn.nn project"
    depends: ["nn.pli"]

    features: [
        "Time crystal neurons: 11 nested phase membranes with closed tick loop",
        "Singularity-reseeded clocks (clocking never damps)",
        "Prime-indexed weights and PPM prime-signature gating",
        "Phase-gated activations (sigmoid, tanh, relu) and phase encoding",
        "Resonance coupling between layers (match -> exchange, mismatch -> dissipate)",
        "Temporal backpropagation: gradients as phase corrections on the 11-cycle",
        "Temporal coherence criterion: circular-distance loss, coherence metric",
        "Phase-aligned training loop with coherence-threshold early stop"
    ]

    models: [
        "XOR time crystal network",
        "Binary crystal classifier",
        "Multi-class crystal classifier"
    ]
}

/*
 * USAGE NOTES:
 *
 * This module adapts nn.pli from standard neurons to time crystal neurons:
 *
 * 1. A neuron is not a point unit but an 11-dimensional time crystal: 11
 *    nested phase membranes whose tick pulse falls one dimension per step
 *    and wraps at d11 back to the rim — a closed time loop, reseeded by a
 *    singularity point so the clocking never damps.
 * 2. Information is carried in the TIME domain: inputs can be encoded as
 *    firing phases on the 11-cycle (phase_encoder) and activations only
 *    leave the neuron when its clock is at the rim (phase 0).
 * 3. Weights carry PPM prime indices; each neuron's prime signature (the
 *    product of its synapse primes) gates its output against the layer
 *    broadcast tick — the neuron fires only on resonant ticks.
 * 4. Layers couple by resonance: frequency match exchanges in-phase ticks,
 *    mismatch dissipates into the parent membrane.
 * 5. Backpropagation becomes temporal: gradients update weights on resonant
 *    ticks and apply phase corrections around the closed loop; error is the
 *    circular distance on the 11-cycle (temporal coherence criterion).
 *
 * Shared time-crystal skin and prime alphabet are inlined by convention from
 * psystems/common/time_crystal_core.pli and psystems/common/alphabet_primes.pli
 * (P-Lingua has no import of those files; see psystems/README.md).
 *
 * This is a conceptual implementation showing how time crystal neural
 * network operations can be expressed in membrane computing formalism.
 */
